{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quark-antiquark-production","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:quark-antiquark-production","kind":"definition","title":"Quark--antiquark production from pair creation","tags":["quark","antiquark","pair-production","hopf-link","meson","hecke-algebra","colored-photon"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.QuarkAntiquarkProduction","text":"quark-antiquark-production.md","leanSource":"quark-antiquark-production.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:quark-antiquark-production\"></a><p><em>A <strong>quark--antiquark production</strong> is the full chain <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma\\gamma \\to q\\bar{q}</code>, in which two colored photons collide and their Hecke-algebra product reduces to a quark--antiquark channel. Each photon is the Hecke algebra element:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">\\gamma = \\mathbf{1} + \\varphi_0\\sigma_0 + \\varphi_1\\sigma_1 + \\varphi_{01}\\sigma_0\\sigma_1^{-1}</code></pre>\n<p><em>with independent color weights <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi_0, \\varphi_1, \\varphi_{01}</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/quark-antiquark-production.md","heading":"Definition","number":"9.2.7","page":"b/def-quark-antiquark-production","qa":{"counts":{"pass":81,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":65},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.QuarkAntiquarkProduction","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/quark-antiquark-production.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
